B.bgt=new A.ae("How do I scan my notes?","Tap the camera button in the middle of the bottom bar. On Android the Smart Scanner finds the page edges for you; the app's own camera finds them too (see below), and you can drag the four corners if they're off. Scan several pages and tap Next: their text is read while you watch (by Claude with Smart Study, else on your phone). Pick a folder and they are saved as notes in its Notebook, titled from their first line. From a note, tap Edit to fix a word or Make Flashcards to turn it into cards.")
B.bfE=new A.ae("How does the app find the page edges?","The app's own camera and gallery import use AI models that run on your phone (no internet, and your photos stay on it), so they work the same on every phone, with or without Google services, and in the browser. If the corners aren't right, drag them. The models are DocAligner by Ze Yuan (DocsaidLab), github.com/DocsaidLab/DocAligner.")
B.bfX=new A.ae("Can the app read the text in my photos?",'Yes. Your phone finds the lines of text first (they light up in blue). With Smart Study on, Claude then reads each page from its photo, which works much better on handwriting; without internet, or with Settings \u2192 Smart Study \u2192 Read Photos with Claude off, the text is read on your phone only. The note opens on its text: tap Edit to fix a misread word, and Make Flashcards to turn it into cards. Your photos stay one tap away. Without Smart Study, cards are suggested from lines like "Term: definition" for you to add or skip.')
B.bgw=new A.ae("Do I need an account?","No. The first time you use Smart Study, the app makes a tAsikaso account for you, without a name or email, with a daily allowance of Claude: pages read, study kits and quizzes, answer checks. Continue with Google (Profile \u2192 Backup & Sync) for more each day, and your name, photo, settings, tasks and Pomodoro statistics are kept in your account: Log Out clears them from the phone and Continue with Google brings them back, on any phone. tAsikaso+ gets the most. Notes and flashcards stay on your phone (back them up with Backup & Sync). Settings \u2192 Smart Study shows today's use, and Settings \u2192 Your Data \u2192 Delete Account deletes the account.")
B.bgv=new A.ae("Where are my notes, and where do my flashcards go?","When you save notes you pick a folder (or make one), and they go in that folder's Notebook: open the folder, then Notebook. When you tap Make Flashcards on a note you pick where the cards go: a new set in any folder, or a set you already have.")
B.bgu=new A.ae("Can I turn a PDF into notes or flashcards?","Yes. Tap + and choose Import PDF (or the PDF button on the camera screen), then save it as Text Notes or flashcards. Lecture slides and handouts work everywhere; scanned PDFs are read on Android and iOS. The first 30 pages are read. To add cards to a set you already have, open the set and choose Make Cards from a PDF.")
B.bfV=new A.ae("What is Smart Study?","With a study server set up in Settings \u2192 Smart Study, Claude (an AI by Anthropic) types up your notes and writes a summary, key concepts, flashcards and quizzes. The photos of your pages (with Read Photos with Claude on), the text read from them, your cards and your typed quiz answers go to your study server and on to Anthropic, and are not kept there. Turn Read Photos with Claude off to send text only. It needs internet; without it, scanning, cards and quizzes still work on the phone.")
B.bfY=new A.ae("How do quizzes work?","Any set with two or more cards has Take a Quiz: multiple choice, true or false, fill in the blank and typed answers. New Quiz lets you pick how many questions and which types. Typed answers forgive spelling slips; with Smart Study on they are judged by meaning. A partly right answer counts as half.")
B.bgq=new A.ae("How does the Pomodoro timer work?","Focus for one Pomodoro (25 minutes by default), then take a short break. After every few Pomodoros you get a long break. Finished Pomodoros count toward the current task and your daily goal. You can change all the lengths in Settings.")
B.bfK=new A.ae("What is Focus Mode?","Pressing START opens a full-screen timer with nothing else on it. Close it with the \u2715 to pause the timer, then press RESUME to carry on.")
B.bfR=new A.ae("How is my streak counted?","Each day you finish a Pomodoro or review flashcards adds a day. Miss a whole day and the streak starts again.")
B.bfN=new A.ae("What happens when a Pomodoro or break ends?","Settings \u2192 When Time Is Up: Alarm Clock (your phone's alarm sound), Vibration Only, Alarm Clock and Vibration, or Off. The alarm rings on the alarm volume, so it works even when the phone is on silent, and keeps ringing until you tap the alert, for up to a minute. It sounds even when the app is closed.")
B.bge=new A.ae("Why didn't I get a notification?","Check that When Time Is Up isn't Off in Settings and that notifications are allowed for the app in your phone's settings. Some phones delay alerts to save battery; allowing \"Alarms & reminders\" for the app makes them exact.")
B.bgm=new A.ae("How does Smart Review work?","Each flashcard comes back when you are about to forget it. A card you know comes back after a growing gap (1, 3, 7, 14 days and so on); a card you miss comes back tomorrow. A set shows how many cards are due today, and you can always study all of them.")
B.bfJ=new A.ae("What does tAsikaso+ add, and can I try it?","tAsikaso+ adds every week, month and year in Pomodoro Analysis with the heatmap and full timeline, smart review, app colors, Google Drive sync and backup files, and unlimited suggested cards (the free plan gets 20 a month). While payments are being set up, every plan is free to try: open Profile \u2192 See Plans, pick Monthly, Semester or Yearly, switch whenever you like, or tap Go Back to Free Plan. Nothing is deleted when a plan ends.")
B.bgi=new A.ae("Where is my data saved?","Everything is saved on this phone; deleting the app deletes it. To keep a copy, open Profile \u2192 Backup & Sync: sync to your Google Drive, or tap Back Up Now for a backup file (both tAsikaso+). Restoring on any phone from the same screen is free. Your study server's app token is never in a backup.")
